      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:2:49:5",
      "text": [
        " كَانَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( صلوات الله عليه )  يَقُولُ اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الِاحْتِلَامِ وَ مِنْ سُوءِ الْأَحْلَامِ وَ أَنْ يَلْعَبَ بِيَ الشَّيْطَانُ فِي الْيَقَظَةِ وَ الْمَنَامِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from his father, from Abdullah Bin Maymoun, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Amir Al-<span class=\"iTxt\">Momineen</span><sup>asws</sup> used to say: ‘O Allah<sup>azwj</sup>! I seek Refuge with You<sup>azwj</sup> from the wet dreams and the evil dreams, and that the Satan<sup>la</sup> would play with me<sup>asws</sup> during the wakefulness and the sleep’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from his father from ‘Abd Allah ibn Maymun from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “Amir al-Mu’minin, Ali ibn abu Talib (a.s.) would say, ‘O Lord, I seek protection with You against wet dreams and bad dreams and from Satan playing with me during my sleep or when awake.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
